--- OUT --->
4
4
0
--- RAST --->
// the constructor hands `$this` back twice and destroys it neither time. CHECK-NOT is scoped between
// the two surrounding CHECKs, so it asserts about the body between the early return and the implicit
// one rather than about the file - the destructor calls at file scope are `$four` and `$empty`
CHECK: function Buffer
CHECK: return(varref<Buffer>(var($this)))
CHECK-NOT: call destructor(addrof<Buffer&>(varref<Buffer>(var($this))))
CHECK: return(varref<Buffer>(var($this)))
// and the two locals are destroyed once each, in reverse declaration order
CHECK: call destructor(addrof<Buffer&>(varref<Buffer>(var($four))))
CHECK: call destructor(addrof<Buffer&>(varref<Buffer>(var($empty))))
